<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan central bank ends control of United Bank.</title>
<headline>Pakistan central bank ends control of United Bank.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's central bank, The State Bank of Pakistan (SBP), said on Monday it was no longer in control of state-owned United Bank Ltd (UBL).</p>
<p>The SBP took over the UBL on April 20, 1996 saying it was losing about 700 million rupees ($20 million) a year from widespread abuses.</p>
<p>The SBP has asked the Ministry of Finance to appoint a UBL president and members of the board of directors, an SBP statement said.</p>
<p>The UBL was taken over after its sale to a Saudi group fell through early last year.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
